 "manifesto": "<b>Read this first.</b> Every place in this guide is niche and non-touristy by design. There are no Dotonbori, Shibuya Crossing, Takeshita-dori, Nishiki souvenir stalls, Golden Pavilion or dinner shows; this is where the scenes themselves shop, drink, dig and play. Many of these rooms are tiny, local and run by one or two people, so go quietly, follow the house rules and keep groups small. The reason these places still feel like this is that most visitors never find them.",
 "discovery": "Discovery cross-check: <a href=\"https://www.corner.inc/\">corner.inc</a>, the Gen-Z place-curation app, for <a href=\"https://www.corner.inc/guides/tokyo\">Tokyo</a>, <a href=\"https://www.corner.inc/guides/osaka\">Osaka</a> and <a href=\"https://www.corner.inc/guides/kyoto\">Kyoto</a>.",
